Spheroid imaging export
Filter: {"channel": "golden"}
Images selected: 13; included: 13; missing: 0

Contents
  images/        original files, unchanged, per experiment
  annotations/   VIA json per annotator, only for the selected images.
                 File names start with the annotator's initials, or 'unknown'.
  metadata.csv   one row per image, with the metadata of its well
  dashboard.html charts and thumbnails. Opens by double-click, works offline

Columns in metadata.csv, in file order

Identifiers
  image_file: Path of the image in this zip; empty if it is listed in MISSING.txt
  original_name: File name as on the disk
  experiment: Experiment name from the metadata workbook, or else the folder name
  vid: Video ID. For match_status 'inferred', taken from the experiment
  well: Plate position
  field: Field number from the file name

Time and image
  timepoint_minutes: Elapsed time from the file name, in minutes
  day: timepoint_minutes / 1440
  channel: Prefix in the file name (BF, Brightfield, PC, Phase), or else the file type
  channel_norm: channel with one name per channel: Brightfield is BF, Phase is PC
  variant: Suffix in the file name, for example masks
  match_status: matched, inferred (VID taken from the experiment), unmatched or ambiguous

Annotations
  regions_AA: Number of regions from annotator AA; 0 means annotated, no regions found; empty means not annotated by them
  regions_unknown: Number of regions from annotator unknown; 0 means annotated, no regions found; empty means not annotated by them
  regions_total: Sum over annotators. Their regions can overlap, so this is not a number of distinct clusters. Empty if the image has no annotation

Treatment
  treatment_raw: Treatment as written in the workbook
  treatment_norm: Normalised treatment; combinations separated by ';'. ABT-199 is written as venetoclax
  concentration: As written in the workbook; combinations follow the treatment order
  concentration_unit: Unit of the concentration; differs between sheets. Empty without a concentration
  stimulation: Stimulation as written in the workbook
  stimulation_norm: Normalised stimulation; combinations separated by ';'
  tissue: Tissue

Sheet-specific columns follow, as written in the workbooks. Sheets differ, so many
are empty for part of the rows. A repeated header in a sheet has the suffix _2.
Headers that differ only in spelling or capitals between sheets share one column
here, for example 'Specific Lysis (%)' and 'Specific lysis (%)'.
Descriptions come from the Legend sheet in the lab's workbooks.

Flow and well results
  proliferation index (CLL): no description in the lab sheet
  proliferation index (CLL)_2: no description in the lab sheet
  Specific lysis (%): no description in the lab sheet
  Target: no description in the lab sheet
  Viability (%): Percentage of live cells

Patient and clinical
  Sample date: no description in the lab sheet

Note
  well_note: Free text found in a cell where a value belongs, as '<column>: <text>'. The text is moved here from that column and is otherwise as written in the sheet

Technical
  file_status: included, or why the file could not be read
  source_zip: Zip on the disk
  source_member: Path inside that zip
  source_workbook: Metadata workbook of the well; empty if the image has no well
  source_sheet: Sheet in that workbook
  source_row: Row in that sheet
  volgnummer: Coded patient / blood-draw number
